  "steps": [
    "Boil the soya granules for 4–5 minutes, then drain and squeeze out all the excess water.",
    "Add the boiled soya, peas, coriander, onion, garlic, green chillies, roasted besan, and all the spices to a mixer. Pulse until it forms a coarse dough.",
    "Shape the mixture into cutlets using lightly greased hands.",
    "Grind the whole wheat bread into fine breadcrumbs and coat each cutlet evenly.",
    "Heat a pan, grease it with 1–2 tsp ghee, and cook the cutlets on low to medium heat for 20–25 minutes, turning occasionally until golden brown and crispy.",
    "Mix the Greek yogurt, grated beetroot, dried mint, rock salt, and chaat masala until smooth. Serve chilled with the crispy cutlets."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The cutlets are pan-cooked; the caption calls them air fryer friendly but gives no air fryer method."
